#hasheq((content-digest . "888206d50bb9de717a465ee6a2e0d7957f08d9fbda4f1d5cacdd0a6aba9a39eb") (report . "I read the full current-head artifacts in /home/user/src/q-agent/q at ref campaign/v1.00.30-w3, whose reflog confirms HEAD = 08175ee9da9cc75dbc9b67401901b48cfb1c37fa (the two fix commits c5eefb16 'repair CLI and multi-zo checkout restore' and 9b22169a/08175ee9 sit directly on the declared head). I read ci/prepared-environment/compiled-root.rkt (producer+resolver), ci/prepared-environment/compiled-root-manifest.rkt (pure validation), scripts/ci/compiled-root.rkt (CLI), tests/test-compiled-root.rkt, tests/test-compiled-root-manifest.rkt, docs/reports/TRUSTED-COMPILED-ROOT-v1.00.30.md, and the three artifacts under artifacts/ci-recovery/v1.00.30-w3, plus README and the tier-ownership files. All four specific claims hold by code inspection. (1) The CLAIM-1 defect is gone: the build branch binds `manifest` to the hash returned by `build-compiled-root!` and passes it directly to `publish-compiled-root!`; no struct accessor (e.g. compiled-root-manifest) is applied anymore, and the printed reason uses `(reason->string #t)` rather than touching the hash. (2) The CLI parses its documented order: `split-dashdash` first extracts the `--` tail into `child-args` from the raw argv, then `ordered-argv` moves the leading `build`/`run` token to the end before `command-line #:argv`, so flags preceding the subcommand are parsed rather than aborting at the first non-flag; the subcommand ends up as the sole `#:args rest` positional and is recovered via `(member (first args) '(\"build\" \"run\"))`. The `run` path forwards `child-args` to both `launch-with-root` and the eager-fallback `system*/exit-code`, so args after `--` reach the child. (3) The producer deletes each created `compiled/` directory exactly once: the per-zo parents are wrapped in `remove-duplicates` before the `unless (member compiled-dir pre-existing-compiled-dirs) (delete-directory/files compiled-dir)` loop, so a module whose in-checkout closure puts several zos in one directory no longer double-deletes (and `collect-checkout-compilation-pairs` genuinely harvests the whole closure). Pre-existing compiled dirs are correctly left untouched. (4) Both regression tests exist and are named/tagged: 'producer restores a shared compiled dir once for a multi-zo closure (B2)' builds a two-module checkout (multi-a requires multi-b) and asserts >=2 sources plus that the shared compiled/ dir is gone, and 'CLI ''build'' subcommand publishes a compiled root (B1)' invokes the CLI with the documented `build --checkout ... --module ... --staging-dir ... --final-dir ... --label ...` order and asserts exit 0 plus a published manifest.rktd — the latter would fail both on the old accessor crash and on the old arg-order parse failure. I also counted 11 test-cases in test-compiled-root.rkt and 12 in test-compiled-root-manifest.rkt, consistent with the documented 23-case matrix. Cross-checks on committed evidence: SHA256SUMS lists 7b5031...45b4e for identity-matrix.json and 283162...0481 for resolution-proof.json, and the identity-matrix records the eight rejection dimensions while resolution-proof records resolved=true, 1 root hit/0 fallbacks/5748 bytes served and producer-checkout-restored=true. Remaining non-blocking concerns are documentation-acknowledged deferrals, not new defects: the TOCTOU guard keys by symlink-resolved `simplify-path` so a symlinked checkout path could cause the wrapper to no-op (recorded for W4); the resolver mutates consumer source mtimes as defense-in-depth (field name `zo-mtime-ms` actually holds seconds); `with-compiled-root` does not restore the original `current-load` after the thunk; `sources[].bytes` is shape-validated only (the manifest module validates source digests elsewhere/resolve-time, so this is a benign dead field); and the reference digests (888206d5..., 34 passed tests, 1201/1201 files, 17892/17892 tests, lint 5/5) were not independently recomputed because I am read-only and cannot run commands — I found nothing in the read code or committed artifacts that contradicts them. Verdict rationale: the two previously blocking defects are demonstrably fixed at the declared head with dedicated regression tests that would fail on the old behavior, the documented CLI/arg contracts are honored, and no new blocking issues surfaced; the residual items are explicitly deferred to W4 and do not compromise the prototype's offline safety contract.") (reviewed-sha . "08175ee9da9cc75dbc9b67401901b48cfb1c37fa") (reviewer . "independent read-only reviewer subagent (fresh non-author, reviewer role, model deepseek/deepseek-v4.1-flash)") (scope . "full implementation diff origin/main...HEAD for W3 trusted compiled-root prototype at reanchored head 08175ee9 (reviewed commit chain: 3dc85933 checkpoint, 9b22169a reanchor, c5eefb16 review fixes, 08175ee9 report/evidence): ci/prepared-environment/compiled-root.rkt; ci/prepared-environment/compiled-root-manifest.rkt; ci/prepared-environment/manifest.rkt; scripts/ci/compiled-root.rkt; tests/test-compiled-root.rkt; tests/test-compiled-root-manifest.rkt; docs/reports/TRUSTED-COMPILED-ROOT-v1.00.30.md; artifacts/ci-recovery/v1.00.30-w3/*; README metrics and tier-ownership regeneration; schema-2 evidence and validation records") (timestamp . "2026-09-19T16:18:57") (verdict . "APPROVED"))
